      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Doorstep Delivery Handover, Inventory Verification &amp; Placement at Kollam</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Upon arrival at the Kollam site, the delivery team must first confirm that the consignment is being received during daylight hours to ensure optimal visibility for inspection. The driver presents the original inventory bilty, and the on‑site coordinator cross‑checks each line item against the physical cartons.</p>
<p>Any discrepancy—missing, damaged, or surplus items—must be recorded immediately in the delivery log and reported to the project manager before uncrating begins. This daylight verification safeguards against loss and provides a clear audit trail for the client.</p>

<p>Once the inventory is verified, the uncrating process starts with a systematic opening of each box, beginning with the heaviest mechanical components followed by delicate electrical units. Every electrical item is plugged into a portable test unit to confirm power continuity, correct voltage, and functional operation.</p>
<p>Mechanical parts are inspected for structural integrity, alignment, and any transport‑induced deformation. Any fault discovered at this stage triggers a “stop‑and‑report” protocol, where the item is isolated, photographed, and a replacement request is filed.</p>

<p>After successful testing, the team proceeds to the clean placement of furniture and equipment. Surfaces are wiped with a lint‑free cloth and a mild, non‑abrasive cleaner to remove dust from packaging.</p>
<p>Items are positioned according to the layout plan, ensuring proper spacing for ventilation of electrical appliances and ergonomic alignment of workstations. The placement sequence follows a logical flow—from larger structural pieces to smaller accessories—to maintain an organized work environment and reduce the risk of accidental damage.</p>

